# CRM — project overview

An open-source, agentic-first CRM. The durable research agent is the product;
the database is where it writes things down. Single-tenant and internal by
design (Google sign-in + one allow-list).

## Monorepo layout (Turborepo on Bun)

| Path            | What it is                                              |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| `apps/agent`    | The research agent — tools, skills, schedules, sandbox |
| `apps/app`      | Next.js front end · http://localhost:3000              |
| `apps/api`      | NestJS API — HTTP, auth, tRPC, Google sync · :3001     |
| `packages/db`   | Prisma schema, migrations, shared Postgres client      |
| `packages/auth` | Better Auth config and the sign-in allow-list          |
| `packages/ui`   | shadcn/ui components, the Tailwind theme               |
| `packages/env`  | Finds and loads the root `.env`                        |

## Three rules the codebase holds to

- **Intelligence never lives in the API** (`docs/api.md`). Nest reports that
  something happened by writing a queue row; the agent decides what it means.
  A Nest service that calls an enrichment API is treated as a bug.
- **`packages/ui` is the only source of UI** (`docs/design.md`). No overriding
  styles at the call site.
- **There are no organizations.** Single tenant, deliberately. Do not add an
  `organizationId`.

## The agent's own rule

Nothing about a person is guessed. No tool accepts a confidence score. Tools
report what they observed; a ledger prices the evidence. Strong evidence writes
to the record, weak evidence becomes a suggestion a human settles.

